    "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0926-0826&BRID=363239&lang=1": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Coordinator, Alumni Engagement Alumni Engagement Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: October 8, 2026 Job Number: J0926-0826 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 6 Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $53,627.97 - $64,618.30/Year Position Description Job Summary The Coordinator, Alumni Engagement actively participates in developing strategic initiatives to encourage continued alumni engagement for more than 57,000 UFV alumni. This position plays a key role in supporting the development of a passionate, connected community of UFV Alumni. The Coordinator uses extensive knowledge of alumni within key alumni markets to implement the defined plan to increase alumni engagement. The Coordinator is responsible for producing marketing and communications materials related to alumni events, programs and activities. The Coordinator supports assigned Alumni related events and projects from the idea phase to implementation. The incumbent provides administrative support for the Director, Alumni Engagement as well as the Alumni Association Board of Directors. Qualifications Diploma in an applicable discipline (e.g., communications, business administration, marketing) from a recognized post-secondary institution. Minimum three (3) years of experience in a post-secondary or similarly complex organizational environment. Excellent communications skills, both oral and written, demonstrating a superior command of the English language. Excellent writing and copy-editing skills with a passion for engaging storytelling. Exceptional organizational abilities, planning skills and attention to detail. Ability to work under pressure, multi-task, manage competing priorities, work to deadlines and make quick, appropriate decisions when challenged. Ability to work independently with minimum supervision. Strategic thinker with superior analytical and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to stay current and adapt to change. Demonstrates creativity and initiative thinking. Ability to address complex/sensitive matters and maintain confidentiality. Ability to exercise mature judgement, initiative and independence in setting and accomplishing goals and priorities. Excellent knowledge and proven experience with MS Office suite. Familiarity with various digital platforms such as Graduway, Blackbaud NetCommunity, Raiser’s Edge database is an asset. Event management experience is an asset. Responsible, outgoing, enthusiastic team player who is results-oriented and dedicated to team success. Adept at building and leveraging a network of relationships to achieve goals. Project management experience, including project coordination, is an asset. Practical understanding of content management systems, including maintenance of existing content, form management, and creation of new posts, pages, and events. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'eméylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in Stó:lo Tém:éxw (Stó:lo Land; Stó:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the Stó:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW — which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
    },
    "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0726-0709&BRID=358195&lang=1": {
      "title": "Sessional Instructor, School of Health Studies",
      "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Sessional Instructor, School of Health Studies Office of the Dean Chilliwack (CEP) Job Number: J0726-0709 Status: Sessional Open Positions: 9 Salary Schedule: Sessional Salary Schedule, Group A Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $8,104.04 - $8,319.55/Section Job Summary The School of Health Studies, part of the Faculty of Health Sciences, offers a range of nursing program options that create exciting opportunities for teaching and academic engagement. The Faculty is recognized for delivering high-quality educational experiences and producing graduates who are in high demand. Located on a technologically advanced campus within the Canada Education Park, the School of Health Studies fosters innovation in teaching and provides access to cutting-edge simulation learning environments. The School of Health Studies requires temporary/sessional faculty to teach in the following program areas: Bachelor of Science in Nursing program: The BSN program offers a four-year program stream and a 2.5 year LPN Access to BSN stream. The BSN program requires part-time/sessional faculty for clinical instruction in the areas of gerontology, medical-surgical, home health, mental health, public health, pediatrics, and child-bearing families. Successful candidates will hold a Baccalaureate degree in nursing and have a strong related clinical practice foundation. A master’s degree is preferred. Practical Nursing program: The PN program requires part-time/sessional faculty for clinical instruction in gerontological, medical and surgical practice settings. Successful candidates will hold a Baccalaureate degree in nursing and a strong related clinical practice foundation. Candidates with a diploma in nursing with extensive clinical practice experience will be considered. Health Care Assistant program: The HCA program requires part-time/sessional faculty for instruction in gerontological practice settings. Successful candidates will hold a Baccalaureate degree in nursing and a strong related clinical practice foundation. Candidates with a diploma in nursing with extensive clinical practice experience will be considered. NOTE: Current BCCNM registration in good standing without limits or conditions, or eligibility for registration with BCCNM prior to start of sessional faculty position is a requirement. How to Apply Please submit the required documents through the online application portal: Cover letter with the program of interest clearly indicated Resume/CV About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'eméylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in Stó:lo Tém:éxw (Stó:lo Land; Stó:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the Stó:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW — which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
